  ('8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$Consider the phrase 'Vistas Walk on the ocean.' How does this title (if it's a title) or introductory phrase set the tone for the subsequent narrative?$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true);
INSERT INTO public.question_bank (id, institution_id, subject_id, topic_id, grade_level_id, class_group_id, question_text, question_type, options, correct_answer, marks, difficulty_level, tags, source, created_by, is_approved, parent_question_id, sub_question_count, sequence_order) VALUES
  ('a73f75ac-9cd4-4fd0-b6e5-11258cc1ed3e', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$EARLY this year, I found myself aboard a Russian research vessel — the Akademik Shokalskiy — heading towards the coldest, driest, windiest continent in the world: Antarctica. My journey began 13.09 degrees north of the Equator in Madras, and involved crossing nine time zones, six checkpoints, three bodies of water, and at least as many ecospheres. By the time I actually set foot on the Antarctic continent I had been travelling over 100 hours in combination of a car, an aeroplane and a ship; so, my first emotion on facing Antarctica’s expansive white landscape and uninterrupted blue horizon was relief, followed up with an immediate and profound wonder. Wonder at its immensity, its isolation, but mainly at how there could ever have been a time when India and Antarctica were part of the same landmass. Part of history Six hundred and fifty million years ago, a giant amalgamated southern supercontinent — Gondwana — did indeed exist, centred roughly around the present-day Antarctica. Things were quite different then: humans hadn’t arrived on the global scene, and the climate was much warmer, hosting a huge variety of flora and Reprint 2026-27$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 20, NULL),
  ('c8a99ad4-74a1-400c-bfea-67150f5c2777', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$For 500 million years Gondwana thrived, but around the time when the dinosaurs were wiped out and the age of the mammals got under way, the landmass was forced to separate into countries, shaping the globe much as we know it today.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('67b72b3d-5cb8-4450-b3a8-38282ef09b0f', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$Imagine: India pushing northwards, jamming against Asia to buckle its crust and form the Himalayas; South America drifting off to join North America, opening up the Drake Passage to create a cold circumpolar current, keeping Antarctica frigid, desolate, and at the bottom of the world.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('40d5ba57-66f4-477d-a74f-c9a97287ade2', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$To visit Antarctica now is to be a part of that history; to get a grasp of where we’ve come from and where we could possibly be heading. It’s to understand the significance of Cordilleran folds and pre-Cambrian granite shields; ozone and carbon; evolution and extinction.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('b6f57310-4605-4de6-82ff-6ad82e74883f', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$For a sun-worshipping South Indian like myself, two weeks in a place where 90 per cent of the Earth’s total ice volumes are stored is a chilling prospect (not just for circulatory and metabolic functions, but also for the imagination). It’s like walking into a giant ping-pong ball devoid of any human markers — no trees, billboards, buildings. You lose all earthly sense of perspective and time here.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 4, NULL),
  ('a715975f-6f77-4142-bb4c-bf47afd264f2', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$When you think about all that can happen in a million years, it can get pretty mind-boggling.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 2, NULL),
  ('04ead3d8-5fbc-486f-8327-8857b7d3e351', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$It’s like walking into a giant ping-pong ball devoid of any human markers — no trees, billboards, buildings.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 2, NULL),
  ('abf3a8e9-786a-4ef4-aeab-52c17efec47b', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$You lose all earthly sense of perspective and time here. The visual scale ranges from the microscopic to the mighty: midges and mites to blue whales and icebergs as big as countries.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
  ('51aea20c-201f-49a9-acf2-77c4749ee21e', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'f1946e0e-32ca-4cf0-86d5-134ac543faa5', '39c6c5a7-f3e7-4070-a1e4-1220b68775f5', 'c714d675-9f79-4969-aa3e-70bc893fc2e7', '4b2248fa-831d-47df-8ee2-e7a1722b39f6', $qbx$For 500 million years Gondwana thrived, but around the time when the dinosaurs were wiped out and the age of the mammals got under way, the landmass was forced to separate into countries, shaping the globe much as we know it today.$qbx$, 'long_answer'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-06-08T09-55-16-399Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 3, NULL),
